---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Terms of Service" description="Monadic Labs terms of service.">
  <section class="container mx-auto max-w-2xl px-5 py-16 sm:py-20">
    <p class="font-mono text-sm text-blue-400">~/terms$</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 font-display text-3xl font-semibold">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 rounded-md border border-amber-500/40 bg-amber-500/10 p-4 text-sm text-amber-500">
      Placeholder legal text — this is not legal advice. Have this reviewed by a
      lawyer before publishing, and replace it with terms that match your actual
      contracts and engagement letters.
    </p>
    <div class="markdown mt-8">
      <p>Use of this website is subject to the following terms. Engineering
      services themselves are governed by a separate, signed project agreement —
      not by this page.</p>
      <h2>Website use</h2>
      <p>This site is provided for informational purposes. Content, including
      case studies, may be illustrative or in-progress and should not be relied
      on as a guarantee of specific outcomes.</p>
      <h2>Engagements</h2>
      <p>Any paid engineering work is governed by a separate written agreement
      covering scope, price, timeline, and intellectual property terms.</p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions: <a href="mailto:hello@monadiclabs.com">hello@monadiclabs.com</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
